{
  "iri": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_167308",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": [
    "A 6-(dimethylamino)-4,4-diphenylheptan-3-one that has (<i>S</i>)-configuration. It is the less active enantiomer of methadone and has very little activity on opioid receptors and mainly responsible for the inhibition of hERG K+ channels and thus for cardiac toxicity. The drug is currently under clinical development for the treatment of major depressive disorder."
  ],
